rl":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels/freq3:%20high","name":"freq3: high","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":null},{"id":375501288,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzU1MDEyODg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels/area:%20core","name":"area: core","color":"c7def8","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the framework runtime"}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2016-09-09T21:05:52Z","updated_at":"2019-09-10T04:21:36Z","closed_at":"2016-11-04T17:55:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**I'm submitting a ...**  (check one with \"x\")\n\n```\n[x] bug report => search github for a similar issue or PR before submitting\n[ ] feature request\n[ ] support request => Please do not submit support request here, instead see https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#question\n```\n\n**Current behavior** \n`variable === undefined` is true when `variable` is `null`, and `null === undefined` is true in templates.\n`variable === null` is false (as expected) when `variable` is `undefined`, but `undefined === null` is true.\n\n**Expected behavior**\n`variable === undefined` should evaluate to false when `variable` is `null`, and `null === undefined` should evaluate to false.\n`variable === null` should evaluate to false (as it does) when `variable` is `undefined`, and `undefined === null` should evaluate to false.\n**Reproduction of the problem**\nhttp://plnkr.co/edit/4QQdILnqyswJAXMIPyHK?p=preview\n\n**What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?**\nIt violates common sense in JavaScript and TypeScript to an offensive degree.\n- **Angular version:** 2.0.0-rc.6\n- **Browser:** all \n- **Language:** all\n","closed_by":{"